232
00:17:57,250 --> 00:17:59,780
unless he thought he was getting something back.

233
00:18:02,010 --> 00:18:05,100
- It doesn't matter. - What do you mean it doesn't matter?

234
00:18:05,370 --> 00:18:06,320
I don't want it.

235
00:18:11,350 --> 00:18:12,400
Are you sure?

236
00:18:13,640 --> 00:18:14,930
It's Valyrian steel.

237
00:18:15,250 --> 00:18:16,910
It's wasted on a cripple.

238
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:55,260
Catelyn Stark would be proud.

239
00:18:56,700 --> 00:18:58,090
You kept your vow.

240
00:18:58,980 --> 00:19:00,430
I did next to nothing.

241
00:19:00,430 --> 00:19:02,140
You're too hard on yourself, my lady.

242
00:19:02,140 --> 00:19:03,030
I'm not a...

243
00:19:07,220 --> 00:19:08,620
Thank you, Podrick.

244
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:29,750
Your Grace, there's still no word from the Unsullied.

245
00:19:29,750 --> 00:19:30,680
Soon.

246
00:19:31,510 --> 00:19:33,090
He will come back to you.

247
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:36,340
He'd better.

248
00:19:38,950 --> 00:19:40,200
What happened?

249
00:19:41,700 --> 00:19:43,190
Many things.

250
00:19:46,180 --> 00:19:47,990
Many things?

251
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:50,560
Your Grace.

252
00:20:19,290 --> 00:20:20,220
I wanted you to see it

253
00:20:20,220 --> 00:20:22,350
before we start hacking it to bits.

254
00:21:00,430 --> 00:21:03,020
Well, this is it. All we'll ever need.

255
00:21:09,340 --> 00:21:11,690
There is something else I want to show you, Your Grace.

256
00:21:37,770 --> 00:21:39,850
The children of the forest made these.

257
00:21:40,450 --> 00:21:41,280
When?

258
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:48,750
A very long time ago.

259
00:21:52,960 --> 00:21:54,130
They were right here,

260
00:21:54,920 --> 00:21:56,660
standing where we're standing.

261
00:21:57,750 --> 00:22:01,330
Before there were Targaryens or Starks or Lannisters.

262
00:22:02,760 --> 00:22:05,040
Maybe even before there were men.

263
00:22:05,670 --> 00:22:06,590
No.

264
00:22:17,650 --> 00:22:21,870
They were here together, the children and the First Men.

265
00:22:22,300 --> 00:22:24,660
Doing what? Fighting each other?

266
00:22:35,060 --> 00:22:39,060
They fought together against their common enemy.

267
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:43,550
Despite their differences, despite their suspicions.

268
00:22:46,190 --> 00:22:47,160
Together.

269
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:51,570
We need to do the same if we're going to survive.

270
00:22:55,760 --> 00:22:57,490
Because the enemy is real.

271
00:22:59,480 --> 00:23:01,190
It's always been real.

272
00:23:11,720 --> 00:23:13,240
And you say you can't defeat them

273
00:23:13,240 --> 00:23:15,950
without my armies and my dragons?

274
00:23:17,320 --> 00:23:18,870
No, I don't think I can.

275
00:23:28,140 --> 00:23:29,780
I will fight for you.

276
00:23:30,550 --> 00:23:32,240
I will fight for the North.

277
00:23:36,350 --> 00:23:37,960
When you bend the knee.

278
00:23:44,270 --> 00:23:45,260
My people...

279
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:49,500
won't accept a southern ruler.

280
00:23:49,950 --> 00:23:51,950
Not after everything they've suffered.

281
00:23:55,510 --> 00:23:57,960
They will if their king does.

282
00:23:59,580 --> 00:24:01,580
They chose you to lead them.

283
00:24:02,740 --> 00:24:04,770
They chose you to protect them.

284
00:24:06,590 --> 00:24:10,000
Isn't their survival more important than your pride?

285
00:24:30,090 --> 00:24:31,060
What is it?

286
00:24:32,900 --> 00:24:34,440
We took Casterly Rock.

287
00:24:35,270 --> 00:24:36,470
That's very good to hear.

288
00:24:41,440 --> 00:24:42,420
Isn't it?

289
00:24:50,760 --> 00:24:52,850
You'll want to discuss this amongst yourselves.

290
00:24:52,850 --> 00:24:54,230
- Perhaps... - You will stay.

291
00:24:55,860 --> 00:24:57,200
All my allies are gone.

292
00:24:57,500 --> 00:24:58,250
They've been taken from me

293
00:24:58,250 --> 00:24:59,980
while I've been sitting here on this island.

294
00:24:59,980 --> 00:25:02,390
- You still have the largest armies. - Who won't be able to eat

295
00:25:02,390 --> 00:25:04,730
because Cersei has taken all the food from the Reach.

296
00:25:04,730 --> 00:25:06,850
Call Grey Worm and the Unsullied back.

297
00:25:06,850 --> 00:25:09,580
We still have enough ships to carry the Dothraki to the mainland.

298
00:25:09,580 --> 00:25:11,830
Commit to the blockade of King's Landing.

299
00:25:11,830 --> 00:25:14,670
- We have a plan. It's still the right plan. - The right plan!

300
00:25:15,080 --> 00:25:17,050
Your strategy has lost us Dorne,

301
00:25:17,050 --> 00:25:19,000
the Iron Islands, and the Reach.

302
00:25:19,710 --> 00:25:22,480
- If I have underestimated our enemies... - Our enemies?

303
00:25:22,880 --> 00:25:24,270
Your family, you mean.

304
00:25:25,320 --> 00:25:26,930
Perhaps you don't want to hurt them after all.

305
00:25:36,860 --> 00:25:38,890
Enough with the clever plans.

306
00:25:39,180 --> 00:25:40,600
I have three large dragons.

307
00:25:40,600 --> 00:25:42,470
I'm going to fly them to the Red Keep.

308
00:25:42,720 --> 00:25:43,670
We've discussed this.

309
00:25:43,670 --> 00:25:46,730
My enemies are in the Red Keep.

310
00:25:47,280 --> 00:25:48,880
What kind of a queen am I if I'm not willing to

311
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:50,170
risk my life to fight them?

312
00:25:50,170 --> 00:25:51,470
A smart one.

313
00:25:55,570 --> 00:25:56,890
What do you think I should do?

314
00:26:00,150 --> 00:26:02,040
- I would never presume to... - I'm at war.

315
00:26:02,210 --> 00:26:03,320
I'm losing.

316
00:26:05,640 --> 00:26:07,320
What do you think I should do?

317
00:26:14,310 --> 00:26:16,560
I never thought that dragons would exist again.

318
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:17,610
No one did.

319
00:26:19,930 --> 00:26:21,470
The people who follow you

320
00:26:21,800 --> 00:26:24,610
know that you made something impossible happen.

321
00:26:26,350 --> 00:26:27,790
Maybe that helps them believe

322
00:26:27,790 --> 00:26:30,910
that you can make other impossible things happen.

323
00:26:31,590 --> 00:26:32,800
Build a world that's different

324
00:26:32,800 --> 00:26:35,170
from the shit one they've always known.

325
00:26:37,720 --> 00:26:41,080
But if you use them to melt castles and burn cities,

326
00:26:42,300 --> 00:26:43,500
you're not different.

327
00:26:45,410 --> 00:26:46,830
You're just more of the same.

328
00:27:02,530 --> 00:27:03,760
Don't lunge.

329
00:27:16,580 --> 00:27:18,760
Don't go where your enemy leads you.

330
00:27:20,680 --> 00:27:21,530
Up.

331
00:27:35,800 --> 00:27:36,980
Nice sword.

332
00:27:39,410 --> 00:27:40,990
Very nice dagger.

333
00:27:47,930 --> 00:27:50,810
If they haven't contributed the right amount of grain to the stores,

334
00:27:50,810 --> 00:27:52,950
then I'm afraid they'll have to make due with what they've brought.

335
00:27:52,950 --> 00:27:54,210
We can't...

336
00:27:58,840 --> 00:28:00,170
It's been a while since I trained.

337
00:28:00,170 --> 00:28:02,850
I can go and find the master of arms for you, my lady.

338
00:28:03,360 --> 00:28:04,860
He didn't beat the Hound.

339
00:28:05,840 --> 00:28:06,650
You did.

340
00:28:08,010 --> 00:28:09,380
I want to train with you.

341
00:28:11,710 --> 00:28:14,360
You swore to serve both my mother's daughters,

342
00:28:14,780 --> 00:28:15,730
didn't you?

343
00:28:23,730 --> 00:28:25,020
Move aside, Podrick.

344
00:28:29,850 --> 00:28:32,280
You can't use that, my lady. It's too small.

345
00:28:32,360 --> 00:28:34,510
I won't cut you. Don't worry.

346
00:28:35,780 --> 00:28:37,060
I'll try not to.

347
00:29:53,490 --> 00:29:55,120
Who taught you how to do that?

348
00:29:55,830 --> 00:29:56,780
No one.

349
00:30:31,740 --> 00:30:33,930
- What do you think of her? - Who?

350
00:30:35,850 --> 00:30:38,510
I believe you know of whom I speak.

351
00:30:39,400 --> 00:30:40,760
I think she has a good heart.

352
00:30:41,060 --> 00:30:42,000
A good heart?

353
00:30:42,970 --> 00:30:44,960
I've noticed you staring at her good heart.

354
00:30:45,800 --> 00:30:47,160
There's no time for that.

355
00:30:48,590 --> 00:30:51,220
I saw the Night King, Davos. I looked into his eyes.

356
00:30:52,870 --> 00:30:55,020
How many men do we have in the North to fight him?

357
00:30:55,020 --> 00:30:56,490
10,000? Less?

358
00:30:56,770 --> 00:30:58,610
- Fewer. - What?

359
00:30:58,890 --> 00:31:02,440
Speaking of good hearts... Missandei of Naath.

360
00:31:03,460 --> 00:31:06,050
Ser Davos, Lord Snow.

361
00:31:06,150 --> 00:31:07,860
King Snow, isn't it?

362
00:31:07,960 --> 00:31:09,280
No, that doesn't sound right.

363
00:31:09,280 --> 00:31:11,470
- King Jon? - It doesn't matter.

364
00:31:11,710 --> 00:31:13,800
Forgive me, but may I ask a question?

365
00:31:14,270 --> 00:31:15,230
Of course.

366
00:31:15,650 --> 00:31:20,120
Your name is Jon Snow, but your father's name was Ned Stark?

367
00:31:20,800 --> 00:31:21,960
I'm a bastard.

368
00:31:23,910 --> 00:31:25,980
My mother and father weren't married.

369
00:31:25,980 --> 00:31:27,910
Is the custom different in Naath?

370
00:31:28,520 --> 00:31:29,860
We don't have marriage in Naath,

371
00:31:29,860 --> 00:31:32,900
so the concept of a bastard doesn't exist.

372
00:31:33,540 --> 00:31:35,990
That sounds... liberating.

373
00:31:38,450 --> 00:31:40,200
Why did you leave your homeland?

374
00:31:41,080 --> 00:31:43,070
I was stolen away by slavers.

375
00:31:43,230 --> 00:31:44,340
I'm sorry.

376
00:31:45,250 --> 00:31:47,600
If I may, how did a slave girl

377
00:31:47,600 --> 00:31:50,090
come to advise Daenerys Targaryen?

378
00:31:51,200 --> 00:31:53,750
She bought me from my master and set me free.

379
00:31:53,920 --> 00:31:55,070
That was good of her.

380
00:31:55,810 --> 00:31:58,620
Of course, you're serving her now, aren't you?

381
00:31:59,730 --> 00:32:02,810
I serve my queen because I want to serve my queen.

382
00:32:03,770 --> 00:32:05,890
Because I believe in her.

383
00:32:05,980 --> 00:32:08,610
And if you wanted to sail home to Naath tomorrow?

384
00:32:08,630 --> 00:32:11,880
Then she would give me a ship and wish me good fortune.

385
00:32:13,110 --> 00:32:14,280
You believe that?

386
00:32:15,390 --> 00:32:16,680
I know it.

387
00:32:17,560 --> 00:32:19,860
All of us who came with her from Essos,

388
00:32:19,860 --> 00:32:21,230
we believe in her.

389
00:32:22,200 --> 00:32:23,950
She's not our queen because she's the daughter

390
00:32:23,950 --> 00:32:25,900
of some king we never knew.

391
00:32:27,360 --> 00:32:29,160
She's the queen we chose.

392
00:32:31,790 --> 00:32:33,670
Will you forgive me if I switch sides?

393
00:32:39,220 --> 00:32:40,650
Is that a Greyjoy ship?

394
00:32:58,390 --> 00:32:59,300
Halt!

395
00:33:24,720 --> 00:33:25,540
Jon.

396
00:33:29,310 --> 00:33:30,580
I didn't know you were here.

397
00:33:38,010 --> 00:33:39,360
S-Sansa...

398
00:33:41,820 --> 00:33:42,870
is she all right?

399
00:33:45,440 --> 00:33:46,720
What you did for her...

400
00:33:48,440 --> 00:33:50,650
is the only reason I'm not killing you.

401
00:33:58,900 --> 00:34:01,050
We heard your uncle attacked your fleet.

402
00:34:02,120 --> 00:34:03,360
We thought you were dead.

403
00:34:04,280 --> 00:34:05,170
I should be.

404
00:34:06,030 --> 00:34:06,990
Your sister?

405
00:34:09,150 --> 00:34:10,300
Euron has her.

406
00:34:11,500 --> 00:34:13,670
I came to ask the queen to help me get her back.

407
00:34:17,090 --> 00:34:18,220
The queen is gone.

408
00:34:20,480 --> 00:34:21,430
Where did she go?

409
00:34:23,110 --> 00:34:25,220
Get the horses watered!

410
00:34:42,430 --> 00:34:44,940
All the gold's safely through the gates of King's Landing.

411
00:34:44,940 --> 00:34:45,790
Good.

412
00:34:45,870 --> 00:34:47,370
We need to get the last of these wagons

413
00:34:47,380 --> 00:34:49,470
over the Blackwater Rush before nightfall.

414
00:34:50,030 --> 00:34:51,340
The head of the line is ambushed,

415
00:34:51,340 --> 00:34:53,610
the tail will never be able to reinforce in time.

416
00:34:53,610 --> 00:34:55,260
Well, we are stretched a bit thin.

417
00:34:55,260 --> 00:34:56,400
With your permission,

418
00:34:56,630 --> 00:35:00,370
flogging stragglers has a marked effect on mobility.

419
00:35:01,670 --> 00:35:04,410
Let's give them fair warning first.

420
00:35:04,420 --> 00:35:06,270
These men fought well at Highgarden.

421
00:35:17,440 --> 00:35:19,490
Now, get it on this thing.

422
00:35:19,490 --> 00:35:20,270
Lift!

423
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:26,720
- Ser Jaime. - Rickon.

424
00:35:27,670 --> 00:35:28,500
Dickon.

425
00:35:32,130 --> 00:35:34,100
I hear you fought bravely at Highgarden.

426
00:35:34,700 --> 00:35:35,790
Your first battle?

427
00:35:37,350 --> 00:35:38,130
And?

428
00:35:40,190 --> 00:35:41,260
It was glorious.

429
00:35:41,330 --> 00:35:43,240
Come on, your father's not here.

430
00:35:45,290 --> 00:35:47,510
All my life, we've been pledged to House Tyrell.

431
00:35:48,260 --> 00:35:50,830
I knew some of those men. I hunted with them.

432
00:35:51,480 --> 00:35:52,890
They didn't deserve to die.

433
00:35:54,070 --> 00:35:56,110
But Lady Olenna chose to betray her queen

434
00:35:56,110 --> 00:35:57,860
and support the Targaryen girl.

435
00:35:58,320 --> 00:35:59,460
So here we are.

436
00:36:01,580 --> 00:36:03,370
I didn't expect it to smell like that.

437
00:36:03,420 --> 00:36:05,430
Men shit themselves when they die.

438
00:36:05,670 --> 00:36:07,750
Didn't they teach you that at fancy lad school?

439
00:36:09,450 --> 00:36:11,220
Well, I learned it when I was five.

440
00:36:19,050 --> 00:36:19,830
What?

441
00:36:21,190 --> 00:36:21,970
Listen.

442
00:36:34,490 --> 00:36:37,620
Spears and shields! Spears and shields!

443
00:36:37,620 --> 00:36:39,750
- What is it? - Get in line!

444
00:36:39,750 --> 00:36:42,700
Spears and shields! Spears and shields!

445
00:36:44,520 --> 00:36:46,380
Get in line now!

446
00:36:46,950 --> 00:36:49,740
Form up! Come on, lads!

447
00:36:49,740 --> 00:36:50,870
Guard those wagons!

448
00:36:50,870 --> 00:36:53,590
Form a line! Form a line!

449
00:36:56,780 --> 00:36:58,440
Round those spears!

450
00:37:05,280 --> 00:37:07,320
Shield wall!

451
00:37:08,970 --> 00:37:10,490
Fill the gaps!

452
00:37:10,630 --> 00:37:13,840
- Archers, steady! - Hold together!

453
00:37:13,840 --> 00:37:16,040
- Archers! - Look alive!

454
00:37:16,040 --> 00:37:17,240
Get tight!

455
00:37:17,730 --> 00:37:19,580
Get in line, boys!

456
00:37:20,300 --> 00:37:22,180
- Ready! - Here they come!

457
00:37:47,010 --> 00:37:49,200
Courage, lads! Courage!

458
00:37:49,730 --> 00:37:51,920
Wait! Wait for it!

459
00:37:52,390 --> 00:37:54,760
Spears out!

460
00:37:58,510 --> 00:38:02,350
Spears out! - Steady! Hold the line!

461
00:38:11,940 --> 00:38:14,520
- Get back to King's Landing. - I'm not abandoning my army.

462
00:38:14,520 --> 00:38:16,770
You're the commander, not a damn infantryman.

463
00:38:16,770 --> 00:38:18,910
Those fuckers are about to swamp us.

464
00:38:20,180 --> 00:38:21,500
We can hold them off.

465
00:38:40,030 --> 00:38:41,710
Dracarys!

466
00:39:19,210 --> 00:39:20,640
Hold the line!

467
00:39:21,550 --> 00:39:22,710
Hold!

468
00:39:24,370 --> 00:39:26,720
- Hold it, lads! - Hold the line!

469
00:39:30,120 --> 00:39:31,000
Throw it!

470
00:39:35,410 --> 00:39:36,380
Hold!

471
00:39:58,770 --> 00:39:59,750
Draw!

472
00:40:00,750 --> 00:40:02,040
Loose!

473
00:40:36,880 --> 00:40:39,100
- Archers! - Archers!

474
00:40:39,100 --> 00:40:41,290
Archers, with me!

475
00:40:41,410 --> 00:40:43,880
- Archers, to the line! - To the line!

476
00:40:49,790 --> 00:40:50,980
- Nock! - Nock!

477
00:40:52,430 --> 00:40:53,410
Draw!

478
00:41:03,160 --> 00:41:04,880
- Loose! - Loose!

479
00:41:11,460 --> 00:41:12,510
Run!

480
00:41:24,450 --> 00:41:26,000
Qyburn's scorpion is over there.

481
00:41:26,000 --> 00:41:27,060
Go get it, then.

482
00:41:27,080 --> 00:41:28,940
I can't shoot with one hand.

483
00:41:31,440 --> 00:41:32,290
Come on!

484
00:42:46,570 --> 00:42:47,510
Need help!

485
00:43:49,830 --> 00:43:50,870
Where are you?

486
00:45:01,870 --> 00:45:03,030
Take cover!

487
00:45:59,980 --> 00:46:01,250
Come on, you fucker.

488
00:46:01,380 --> 00:46:02,980
Dracarys.

489
00:47:15,810 --> 00:47:17,330
Flee, you idiot.

490
00:47:18,540 --> 00:47:20,460
Come on, boy. Come on!

491
00:47:29,600 --> 00:47:32,960
You idiot. You fucking idiot.

492
00:49:25,230 --> 00:49:26,890
I'm not here to murder.

493
00:49:27,010 --> 00:49:28,730
Bend the knee and join me.

494
00:49:29,050 --> 00:49:31,780
Or refuse... and die.

